            <title>[LU-21044] sanity-sec test_27ac: MDS LBUG class_free_dev() ASSERTION( obd-&gt;obd_minor == -1 || class_num2obd(obd-&gt;obd_minor) == obd ) on umount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21044</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;MDS crash (LBUG) while unmounting an MDT in sanity-sec test_27ac, DNE ldiskfs el8.10 (review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LustreError: 160972:0:(genops.c:431:class_free_dev()) ASSERTION( obd-&amp;gt;obd_minor == &lt;del&gt;1 || class_num2obd(obd&lt;/del&gt;&amp;gt;obd_minor) == obd ) failed: obd ffff934bbc429638 != obd_devs&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;7&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; 0000000000000000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Trace (umount -d -f /mnt/lustre-mds2, i.e. lustre-MDT0001, while its osp connections to MDT0000 were already failing with -107):&lt;br/&gt;
class_free_dev &amp;lt;- class_unregister_device &amp;lt;- class_detach &amp;lt;- class_process_config &amp;lt;- class_manual_cleanup &amp;lt;- server_put_super &amp;lt;- generic_shutdown_super &amp;lt;- cleanup_mnt&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;class_unregister_device() erased the obd_devs entry and dropped the obd_device_list reference, and that dropped the last reference, so class_free_dev() ran with obd_minor still set and obd_devs&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;7&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; already empty. The "newdev" reference class_detach() drops afterwards must already have been gone, so some other path has put one reference too many on this obd (a refcount imbalance or race during MDT teardown).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen once: lustre-reviews build 134461 (change 67604 patchset 23, which touches only mdd/mdt/llite NO_APPEND handling and nothing in obdclass), test session 62f3ce76-122b-44d7-898c-463707bec595, master, 4.18.0-553.155.1.el8_10_lustre. The same test group passed 1345 of 1345 runs on other changes in the previous 30 days; no other crash with this signature in 30 days.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-67604-ps23-829ab9905bc8 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/67604" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/67604&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
